{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From the first of all the fruit of the ground that you bring from your land.</b> The choicest of all its fruits, as in וְרֵאשִׁית שְׁמָנִים יִמְשָׁחוּ (Amos 6:6), נְקֻבֵי רֵאשִׁית הַגּוֹיִם (Amos 6:1). The choicest are the seven species with which the land of Israel is praised, as transmitted in the tradition. This explains what was commanded above in רֵאשִׁית בִּכּוּרֵי אַדְמָתְךָ תָּבִיא (Exodus 23:19), clarifying that the intent there was that you bring first fruits from the choicest of your land's produce — namely, the seven species with which it is praised (Deuteronomy 8:8–9)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:12.107070988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}